{
  "id": "s03-l01",
  "unit": "s03-vowel-signs",
  "title": "Vowel signs 1: া ি ী",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**Vowels after a consonant are written as signs (কার kar).** Instead of writing ক + আ, you write ক + া = **কা** (`ka`). Now you can read মামা (`mama`), খালা (`khala`), বাবা (`baba`)!\n\n**The big surprise: ি is written BEFORE the consonant.** In কি, the ি hook is drawn on the left, but you still say k first, then i. Read it as 'consonant, then the hook's vowel': চাচি = চা + চি = `chachi`, দাদি = `dadi`.\n\n**ি vs ী**: the short-i sign hooks to the left, the long-i sign hooks to the right (কী). They sound the same; the spelling just differs per word (চাচি with ি, নদী with ী).\n\nTip: the sign া is the same stick that turns অ into আ.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "k-aa",
      "bn": "কা",
      "tr": "ka",
      "en": "া (a-kar): adds 'a' as in 'father' after the consonant",
      "notes": "Bare sign: া (U+09BE), name a-kar (আ-কার). Written to the right of the consonant."
    },
    {
      "id": "k-i",
      "bn": "কি",
      "tr": "ki",
      "en": "ি (i-kar, short-i sign): adds 'i' as in 'see'",
      "notes": "Bare sign: ি (U+09BF), name hroshsho i-kar (হ্রস্ব ই-কার). Typed after the consonant but DRAWN to its left. Same sound as ী."
    },
    {
      "id": "k-ii",
      "bn": "কী",
      "tr": "ki",
      "en": "ী (long-i sign): adds 'i' as in 'see'",
      "notes": "Bare sign: ী (U+09C0), name dirgho i-kar (দীর্ঘ ই-কার). Written to the right. Same sound as ি. কী also means 'what?'"
    },
    {
      "id": "nodi",
      "bn": "নদী",
      "tr": "nodi",
      "en": "river",
      "notes": "Bangladesh is a land of rivers: পদ্মা, মেঘনা, যমুনা."
    }
  ],
